let __v_252 = Value::from("Write it down while it is fresh: date, what was said or done, who saw it. Then tell someone with authority - your manager if it is a colleague, their manager or HR if it is your manager - in writing, asking for a meeting and what you want to change. Keep the tone flat and factual. Your contract and your workplace's grievance policy set out the steps; a free advice line like ACAS or Citizens Advice will tell you where you stand, and you do not have to sort it out before you report it.");
frame.store("_BULLY_REPLY", __v_252.clone())?;
let __v_253 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"going back to work\",\"going back to my job\",\"go back to work\",\"going back to the office\",\"back to work\",\"back at work\",\"back in work\",\"returning to work\",\"return to work\",\"returning to my job\",\"starting back at work\",\"first day back\",\"first day back at work\",\"gone back to work\",\"went back to work\"]}")?;
frame.store("_GOING_BACK", __v_253.clone())?;
let __v_254 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"nervous\",\"anxious\",\"anxiety\",\"worried\",\"worry\",\"dreading\",\"dread\",\"scared\",\"guilty\",\"excited\",\"maternity\",\"paternity\",\"parental\",\"baby\",\"leave\",\"first day\",\"months\",\"exhausted\",\"knackered\",\"shattered\",\"tired\",\"drained\",\"off sick\",\"sick note\",\"signed off\",\"phased\",\"fit note\",\"stress\",\"burnout\",\"depressed\",\"depression\",\"next week\",\"next month\",\"on monday\",\"tomorrow\",\"this week\",\"soon\",\"my wife\",\"my husband\",\"my partner\",\"sickness\",\"illness\",\"unwell\",\"after being ill\",\"time off\",\"hate\",\"hate it\",\"regret\",\"miserable\",\"cant face\",\"can't face\",\"dont want to go back\",\"don't want to go back\",\"do not want to go back\",\"dont want to return\",\"don't want to return\",\"not looking forward\",\"dreading going back\",\"dreading it\",\"cant face going back\",\"can't face going back\"]}")?;
frame.store("_GOING_BACK_LINE", __v_254.clone())?;
let __v_255 = Value::from("Give it six weeks before you judge it: the first weeks back are a bad test of a job, because everything is new, tiring and out of your hands. Write down what is actually wrong - the hours, the manager, the work itself, the money - because the fix is different for each one, and 'I hate it' is too big to ask anybody to solve. If the thing making you dread it is the same thing that made you ill last time, ask your GP for a fit note that says what needs to change; that is what an occupational health referral is for.");
frame.store("_GOING_BACK_WRONG", __v_255.clone())?;
let __v_256 = Value::from("Not wanting to go back is worth taking seriously rather than talking yourself out of: name the one thing you are dreading - the hours, a person, the work itself, the childcare - because the fix is different for each. If it is the hours or the person, ask for the change before the first morning: a phased return, different hours, or a move within the team. If it is the work itself, go back anyway and give it six weeks, because it is much easier to look for another job from inside one than from a gap. Tell one person at home how you feel, so the first week is not being carried alone.");
frame.store("_GOING_BACK_DONT_WANT", __v_256.clone())?;
let __v_257 = Value::from("Sort the dull things before the first morning - the commute, what you are wearing, and who does the nursery run or the school pickup - so the morning is already decided. On day one ask your manager for ten minutes in the first hour: what has changed, what they need from you first, and who to ask about the rest. The first week is names and questions, and asking them is not a weakness in week one.");
frame.store("_GOING_BACK_PREP", __v_257.clone())?;
let __v_258 = { let __v_259 = Value::from("Nerves the week before are normal, and they ease by the end of the first week. "); let __v_260 = frame.load(rt, "_GOING_BACK_PREP")?; pyrt::ops::add(&__v_259, &__v_260)? };
frame.store("_GOING_BACK_NERVES", __v_258.clone())?;
let __v_261 = Value::from("Being this done in by a working day is normal for the first few weeks back, and it passes: a day at work costs more than it used to, and that is the job, not you. Keep the evenings empty for a fortnight, go to bed an hour earlier and take the lunch break away from the desk, because the break is what makes the afternoon work. If six weeks in you are still wrecked, that is worth a word with your GP - and have your blood checked for iron and thyroid.");
frame.store("_GOING_BACK_TIRED", __v_261.clone())?;
let __v_262 = Value::from("You go back to the same job on the same terms if you took 26 weeks of maternity leave or less; past that it is a suitable alternative job on no worse terms, and they have to offer it before anyone else. Ask HR before you go back for your hours and pay confirmed in writing, and if you want different hours put a flexible working request in - they must decide within two months. A keep-in-touch day or two makes the first week much easier, and if you are still feeding, ask where you can express milk and for breaks long enough to do it.");
frame.store("_GOING_BACK_LEAVE", __v_262.clone())?;
let __v_263 = Value::from("Go back in steps rather than all at once: ask for a phased return - shorter days or fewer days for two to four weeks - and say what you can do now rather than what you cannot. Your fit note can say you may be fit for work with changes, and occupational health, where there is one, is there to arrange those, not to judge whether you are ready. Expect the first week to be tiring and keep the evenings clear; a setback is not a relapse.");
frame.store("_GOING_BACK_SICK", __v_263.clone())?;
let __v_264 = Value::from("The first weeks back take it out of the person who is going, and the load lands on the household: take the mornings, the pickups and the cooking for a fortnight without being asked, and ask what would actually help rather than guessing. Expect them to be flat and tired by Thursday for the first month - that is the job, not a problem with them. If they are dreading it, a plan for the first morning helps more than reassurance.");
