let __v_5054 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"redundancy\",\"being made redundant\",\"made redundant\",\"redundant\"]},\"Redundancy is your job going, not you doing anything wrong: the employer needs fewer people in that role, so the role disappears and your contract ends. If you have two years' service you are owed statutory redundancy pay - half a week's pay for each year under 22, a week for each year from 22 to 40, a week and a half for each year over 41, capped at £700 a week and 20 years - plus your notice and any holiday you have not taken.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"how much\",\"how do i claim\",\"claim\",\"my employer\",\"i have been\",\"i was\",\"voluntary\",\"offer\",\"payout\",\"calculate\",\"calculator\",\"notice\",\"letter\",\"consultation\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"performance review\",\"appraisal\",\"one to one\",\"1 to 1\",\"probation review\"]},\"A performance review is the regular sit-down where your manager says how the job is going and what changes, usually once or twice a year, with a rating that decides any pay rise. Go in with three things you did that made a difference and one thing you want to learn, in numbers where you can, and ask for the rating and the pay in the same conversation.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"how do i prepare\",\"prepare\",\"what should i say\",\"nervous\",\"my review\",\"went badly\",\"bad review\",\"salary\",\"pay rise\",\"ask for\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"btec\",\"btecs\",\"btec diploma\",\"btec extended diploma\"]},\"A BTEC is a work-related qualification taken at school or college instead of, or alongside, A levels: the Level 3 Diploma and Extended Diploma are the usual ones and they are graded pass, merit, distinction, distinction star. They are assessed mostly by coursework rather than exams, and universities accept them - a distinction star is worth about an A at A level for entry - so they suit someone who does better on projects than in a three-hour exam.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"how do i\",\"should i\",\"worth it\",\"my\",\"results\",\"grade\",\"ucas\",\"points\",\"apply\",\"college\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"foundation year\",\"foundation course\",\"foundation degree\",\"access course\"]},\"A foundation year is the extra year at the start of a degree for someone without the usual grades or the right subjects: you do a year of the basics, and passing it moves you onto the first year of the degree. It is not the same as a foundation degree, which is a two-year qualification of its own, or an Access course, which is a year at a college for adults going to university.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"how do i\",\"should i\",\"worth it\",\"my\",\"student loan\",\"fees\",\"apply\",\"ucas\",\"which university\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"personal statement\",\"ucas statement\"]},\"A personal statement is the one page - 4,000 characters, about 47 lines - where you say why you want the course and what you have done that shows it: the subject you read round, the work or volunteering, what you want to do after. Write it in plain first person, spend most of it on the course rather than your childhood, and give it to a teacher or someone in the job to read before you send it.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"how do i write\",\"how to write\",\"help me write\",\"start\",\"example\",\"opening\",\"my personal statement\",\"draft\",\"word count\",\"characters\",\"ucas\",\"for a job\",\"job application\",\"job interview\",\"cover letter\",\"applying for a job\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"gcse\",\"gcsEs\",\"gcses\"]},\"GCSEs are the exams most pupils in England, Wales and Northern Ireland take at 16, in eight to ten subjects, graded 9 to 1 (9 is the top, 4 is a standard pass, 5 a strong pass). Maths, English language and science are the ones nearly everyone takes, and the grades decide which sixth form, college course or apprenticeship you can start.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"how do i revise\",\"revise\",\"revising\",\"results\",\"grades\",\"resit\",\"retake\",\"how many\",\"which\",\"choose\",\"my\",\"equivalent\",\"entry requirements\",\"do i need\",\"need to be\",\"need for\",\"to become\",\"to be a\",\"to be an\",\"require\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"a level\",\"a levels\",\"as level\",\"as levels\"]},\"A levels are the two-year exams taken at 16 to 18 in England, Wales and Northern Ireland, usually three subjects, graded A star to E. Each is mostly decided by exams at the end of the second year, and three good A level grades are the standard way into a degree.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"how do i revise\",\"revise\",\"revising\",\"results\",\"grades\",\"resit\",\"retake\",\"how many\",\"which\",\"choose\",\"my\",\"equivalent\",\"entry requirements\",\"ucas points\",\"level 1\",\"level 2\",\"level 3\",\"level 4\",\"level 5\",\"grade\",\"grades\",\"do i need\",\"need to be\",\"to be a\",\"to be an\",\"require\"]}]}]}")?;
