let __v_5185 = Value::from("A paper round is paid per round rather than per hour, usually £10 to £25 a week and paid by the newsagent on the same day each week. Round and round the shops on the way: the ones with their own delivery staff pay a little more than an agency round, and a Sunday-only round is the smallest way to start.");
frame.store("PAPER_ROUND_PAY", __v_5185.clone())?;
let __v_5186 = Value::from("Thirteen is the usual age: the law lets a child work part-time from 13, and below that almost no newsagent will take them on - a few councils allow some jobs from 12, and the council's child employment office will say what yours does. Under 16 they need a work permit from the council, which the newsagent applies for. The hours are capped too: not before 7am or after 7pm, two hours on a school day and 12 hours a week in term time, and up to 35 hours a week in the school holidays.");
frame.store("PAPER_ROUND_AGE", __v_5186.clone())?;
let __v_5187 = Value::from("Let them try a week of it before you decide, because the job is getting up at half six in the rain six days a week whatever the weather, and that is the part worth finding out. A round within walking distance is the one to take: a lift to the start of it at 6.30am quietly ends most paper rounds by half term. The money is small - £10 to £25 a week - so treat it as the lesson in turning up rather than as earnings.");
frame.store("PAPER_ROUND_WHY", __v_5187.clone())?;
let __v_5188 = Value::from("A paper round is a decent first job when the round is short and close to home: it is the lesson in turning up whatever the weather, which is most of what any employer wants, and it pays £10 to £25 a week. The cost is the hour before school, so pick one that can be walked in half an hour and check the homework still fits. Under 16 the newsagent gets a work permit from the council first.");
frame.store("PAPER_ROUND_WORTH", __v_5188.clone())?;
let __v_5189 = Value::from("Ask at the newsagent on your own street first, and take a parent with you the first time: they will want to know your age, and under 16 they apply to the council for your work permit. Say which mornings you can do and stick to them, because the round goes out whether or not you turn up - turning up is the whole of what they are paying you for.");
frame.store("PAPER_ROUND_SELF", __v_5189.clone())?;
